> What is so special about black pudding from sink?

If you hit a black pudding with an iron weapon it
will split into two new black puddings.  Total hit
points are divided into those two so they get
progressively easier to kill.  They don't hit any
weaker, so this quickly becomes dangerous unless
you have a strong character.  Here comes the
special part - Those weak puddings will gradually
heal back up to full strength.  It can make for an
infinite supply of this type of monster if you have
enough patience.  Killing monsters gives experience,
food from the corpses and a chance for randomly
generated items at the time of death.  It takes
*much* patience.  Here comes the other half of the
special part - Get black puddings to a level with
an altar and you have the potential for infinite
sacrafices.

